{"type":"plan","title":"The Mended Kite","logline":"A torn kite, a sailor's seam, and a gold star — love repairs what wind breaks.","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Brighton seafront at morning wind: the pier stretches over shingle beach, sea horizon rippling. Eight-year-old Maya stands on the boards, arms up, flying her red diamond kite high on a taut string. Golden morning light catches the red sail.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"On a windy autumn morning in Brighton, eight-year-old Maya flies her red kite above the pier.","cites":[]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Low angle close-up on the kite as a sudden gust slams it sideways into the pier's wooden railings. The red sail snags and tears with a sharp rip from corner to corner, a jagged hole opening, a flap of red cloth hanging loose, pale sky showing through.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"A gust slams it into the pier railings, and the red sail tears from corner to corner.","cites":[]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Maya runs along the shingle beach toward home, morning wind tugging her yellow raincoat. She hugs the broken kite tight to her chest, the torn sail flap bouncing against her. The pier railings recede behind her.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs home along the seafront, the broken kite hugged to her chest.","cites":[]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Inside the cozy vintage kitchen, morning light streams through lace curtains onto the wooden table. Grandfather sits in his navy cardigan, newspaper half-folded, looking up over brass-rimmed glasses as Maya bursts in. The brass thimble on his chain catches the light.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Her grandfather, who mended sails when he was young, looks up from his newspaper.","cites":[]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Insert shot: the kite laid flat on the wooden table, torn sail spread. Grandfather's hands thread a needle with white sailcloth thread. Morning light highlights the jagged hole and the spool of thread beside a jar.","mode":"still","dialogue":"At the kitchen table he lays the kite flat and threads a needle with sailcloth thread.","cites":[]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Over-the-shoulder","description":"Over Grandfather's shoulder: he guides Maya's small fingers, showing the sailor's seam — tiny even stitches closing the hole. The white cloth patch grows across the tear, stitches visible. Maya watches, rapt.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Stitch by stitch, he shows Maya how a sailor's seam holds against the wind.","cites":[]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Extreme close-up on the patched kite: Maya's brush adds a bold gold star in the center of the white patch. The star shines against the red sail. Morning light still fills the window behind.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Maya paints a small gold star over the patch, so the kite will remember.","cites":[]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Brighton seafront in bright afternoon: Maya and Grandfather walk side by side along the shingle beach toward the pier. Grandfather carries the mended kite under his arm, its starred patch visible. Sea sparkles, wind gentler.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"In the afternoon they walk back to the beach together, the kite under Grandfather's arm.","cites":[]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Low angle on Maya as she sprints into the wind, unreeling string. The starred kite leaps upward, climbing higher than the pier railings, tail bows streaming. Grandfather watches from behind, cardigan fluttering.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs into the wind, and the kite climbs higher than ever over the waves.","cites":[]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Two-shot","description":"Medium two-shot: Maya turns, offering the string spool to Grandfather. He takes it, head thrown back, laughing like a boy — white beard bristling, eyes crinkled. The kite soars above them, string taut.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"She hands the string to her grandfather, and he laughs like a boy.","cites":[]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Golden dusk on Brighton seafront: long shadows stretch across wet sand. Maya and Grandfather walk home along the water's edge, the mended kite resting on Maya's shoulder, gold star catching the last light. Pier lights flicker on.","mode":"still","dialogue":"At golden dusk they walk home along the sand, the mended kite on Maya's shoulder.","cites":[]}]}
